<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#sanctions">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanctions</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sanctions are penalties, usually economic, imposed by states or international bodies to pressure another state to change its behaviour. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1935, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> imposed sanctions on Italy. These measures proved ineffective in halting Italian expansion and exposed the weakness of the League.</p></div>
